// Default editor layout.
//
// Row([..]) lays its children side by side, Col([..]) stacks them. A child
// takes all that is left unless it is wrapped in a size: Fixed(cells) or
// Percent(0..=100), written Fixed(30, child). Only one child of a Row or Col
// may be left without a size.
//
// The explorer's right edge and the terminal's top edge (a bar or a pane with a Fixed or Percent size)
// can be dragged with the mouse. The size holds for the run only: it is not saved, the file is not
// written, and it gives way to the file when the file changes (View: Reset Pane Sizes does too).
//
// A RightBar is a bar to the right of the editor, for a plugin's preview (a plugin placed
// in the "side pane" in Plugins: Manage gets one made for it, 40% of the editor's row, which
// can be dragged wider or narrower). Write one yourself to choose its place and size, for example
// in place of the editor's Pane:
//
//   Row([
//       Pane(view: Editor, sides: [], title: Hidden),
//       Percent(40, RightBar(views: [Plugin("markdown")], hidden: true)),
//   ])
//
// `hidden: true` starts it hidden. "View: Toggle Side Pane" (ctrl+k p) shows and hides it,
// and what you did last time is remembered. It is left out on a screen under 100 columns.
//
// A Pane shows one component: Explorer, Editor, Terminal, StatusBar, MenuBar (the
// row with the menu icon; leave it out for no row) or Plugin("view.id"). A SideBar or a BottomBar holds a list of views (Explorer,
// Errors, Debug, Terminal and Plugin("view.id")) and shows one at a time; with more than one it
// draws their names in the title row, `Files - Git`, the shown one highlighted,
// and a click on a name (or the "Bar: Next View" action) switches. It takes the
// same fields as a Pane except `view`, which is `views: [...]`. A view is listed
// once in the layout. `Pane(view: Explorer)` and `Pane(view: Terminal)` still work
// and are the same as a bar with that one view. Whatever a pane leaves out keeps
// the component's default:
//
//   Pane(
//       view: Explorer,
//       hidden: true,           // starts hidden (false: shown); for the Explorer, Terminal
//                               // and StatusBar (a bar: its first view). What you hid or showed last time is
//                               // remembered (state.json) and wins over this
//       sides: [Top, Right],    // edges with a border line: Top, Right, Bottom,
//                               // Left or All; [] for no border
//       border: Rounded,        // Plain, Rounded, Double, Thick, QuadrantInside,
//                               // QuadrantOutside or a dashed form: Light/Heavy
//                               // + Double/Triple/Quadruple + Dashed
//       title: Text("Files"),   // Hidden, Name (its own name; the file name for
//                               // the editor) or Text("...")
//       title_align: Center,    // Left, Center or Right
//       title_slot: "my.title", // theme slot that styles the title
//       border_slot: "my.edge", // theme slot that styles the border; a focused
//                               // pane uses "<slot>.focused" when the theme has it
//   )
//
// Defaults: panes get a border on all sides, Plain, and their Name; the Editor
// gets the same border and no title (its tab bar names the files); the
// StatusBar has no border.

Col([
    Fixed(1, Pane(view: MenuBar)),
    Row([
        Fixed(30, SideBar(views: [Explorer], sides: [Right], border: QuadrantInside, title: Hidden)),
        Col([
            Pane(view: Editor, sides: [], title: Hidden),
            Fixed(12, BottomBar(views: [Terminal, Errors, Debug], sides: [Top], border: LightDoubleDashed, title: Name)),
            Fixed(1, Pane(view: StatusBar)),
        ]),
    ]),
])
